BODY = f'''
<a class="skip" href="#overview">Skip to review</a>
<aside class="sidebar"><div class="eyebrow">Personal infrastructure</div><div class="brand">Nix Lifestyle</div><div class="small muted" style="color:#a4bfbf">Configuration review · 2026</div><nav aria-label="Report navigation"><a href="#overview">01 &nbsp; Assessment</a><a href="#findings">02 &nbsp; Findings</a><a href="#usage">03 &nbsp; Your workflows</a><a href="#roadmap">04 &nbsp; Work plan</a><a href="#validation">05 &nbsp; Verification</a><a href="#inventory">06 &nbsp; Scope & versions</a><a href="#method">07 &nbsp; Method & limits</a></nav><div class="bottom">Self-contained local report.<br>Review choices stay in this browser.<button id="print-side">Print / save as PDF</button><a class="download" href="report-data.json" download>Download evidence JSON</a><div class="mono">{esc(D['commit'][:12])} + working edits</div></div></aside>
<main class="shell"><div class="topline"><span>26 OCTOBER 2026 · BOTH NIX LAYERS</span><span>PRIVATE LOCAL ARTIFACT · NO HOSTING</span></div>
<header class="hero" id="overview"><div class="eyebrow">An evidence-based review</div><h1>NixOS, from boot<br>to buffer.</h1><p>Your configuration builds a capable development workstation. The best next work is recovery correctness, small integration fixes, and testing the assumptions behind performance tuning.</p><div class="chips"><span>2 independent flakes</span><span>2 LG Gram hosts</span><span>4 reviewers + independent second passes</span><span>Configuration preserved</span></div></header>
<div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>{len(F)}</strong><span>findings & recommendations</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{D['nix_files']}</strong><span>Nix files in scope</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>90,973</strong><span>retained history records analyzed</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>3 / 3</strong><span>configuration dry runs passed</span></div></div>
<div class="callout"><b>One high-priority issue — before a reinstall.</b><p>The shared destructive Disko target is <code>/dev/nvme0n1</code>; the current system is installed on <code>/dev/nvme1n1</code>. Correct stable disk identity and the recovery recipe before using them. Ordinary rebuilds do not repartition either disk. <a href="#SYS-01">Evidence →</a></p></div>
<div class="grid2"><div class="tile"><h3>Fix the small things on the daily path</h3><p>Neovim’s formatter disagrees with the repo policy, its format toggle is inverted, Pi’s Herdr skill link is broken, and a missing tunnel token causes thousands of retries.</p><div class="linkrow"><a href="#ECLI-001">Formatter</a><a href="#ECLI-002">Toggle</a><a href="#AI-002">Skill link</a><a href="#AI-003">Tunnel</a></div></div><div class="tile"><h3>Make trust boundaries explicit</h3><p>Passwordless Nix is root-equivalent. SSH permits password-capable authentication on every interface. Shell token serialization and token-bearing command arguments deserve narrow fixes.</p><div class="linkrow"><a href="#SYS-02">Privilege policy</a><a href="#SYS-03">SSH</a><a href="#AI-001">Shell serialization</a><a href="#AI-008">Tunnel credentials</a></div></div><div class="tile"><h3>Invest where your usage points</h3><p>Git, Neovim, Terraform and Kubernetes dominate recorded work. Terraform/YAML editor support and a reliable update prebuild are stronger candidates than another orchestration layer.</p><div class="linkrow"><a href="#usage">Usage analysis</a><a href="#ECLI-003">Language support</a><a href="#ECLI-005">Update workflow</a></div></div><div class="tile"><h3>Measure tuning; preserve what works</h3><p>Some TLP settings are inert. GPU, Wi-Fi and UCSI logs merit focused tests; they do not prove broad instability. Keep the working kernel path while establishing a tested fallback.</p><div class="linkrow"><a href="#SYS-08">Ineffective power settings</a><a href="#SYS-09">Kernel recovery</a><a href="#DESK-04">Browser experiments</a></div></div></div>
<div class="pass-grid"><div class="pass-tile"><b>✓ NixOS · Gram 17 / 2025</b>Complete toplevel dry run passed<small>Running host also inspected</small></div><div class="pass-tile"><b>✓ NixOS · Gram 14 / 2022</b>Complete toplevel dry run passed<small>Hardware behavior not tested remotely</small></div><div class="pass-tile"><b>✓ Home Manager · nelson</b>Activation-package dry run passed<small>Eight dependency alias deprecations</small></div></div>
<p class="small muted">A dry run evaluates and plans dependencies; it does not compile missing derivations or test activation. The system run plans 47 derivations and one 15.6 KiB fetch. No system changes were activated. Zero failed units coexists with a Herdr service in an automatic restart loop.</p>

<section id="findings"><div class="eyebrow">02 / Evidence and recommendations</div><h2>Findings you can work through</h2><p class="section-intro">Filter by area, priority or type. Each item includes the observed behavior, impact, recommended action, source evidence and verification steps. Open a card to record a decision. These decisions do not change your configuration.</p>
<div class="legend"><span class="badge P1">P1 · {COUNTS['P1']} · address before the stated trigger</span><span class="badge P2">P2 · {COUNTS['P2']} · next focused work or policy decision</span><span class="badge P3">P3 · {COUNTS['P3']} · improvement / investigation</span><span class="badge Info">Info · {COUNTS['Info']} · observation</span></div>
<div class="filters"><label>Search findings<input type="search" id="search" placeholder="Try: kernel, formatter, token, backup…" autocomplete="off"></label><label>Area<select id="group"><option value="">All areas</option>{option_list(sorted(set(f['group'] for f in F)))}</select></label><label>Priority<select id="priority"><option value="">All priorities</option>{option_list(['P1','P2','P3','Info'])}</select></label><label>Type<select id="lens"><option value="">All types</option>{option_list(sorted(set(f['lens'] for f in F)))}</select></label><label>Review state<select id="review-filter"><option value="">Any review state</option><option value="unreviewed">Not reviewed</option><option value="fix">Plan a change</option><option value="investigate">Investigate / measure</option><option value="keep">Keep current choice</option><option value="defer">Defer</option></select></label><label>Local notes<span class="small muted">Saved in this browser. Export for a portable copy.</span></label></div>
<div class="filter-actions"><span id="result-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">{len(F)} findings</span><div class="action-group"><button id="reset">Reset filters</button><button id="expand">Expand visible</button><button id="collapse">Collapse visible</button><button id="export">Export decisions</button><button id="print-main">Print all</button></div></div><p id="save-status" class="status-message" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="finding-list">{''.join(card(f) for f in F)}</div><div id="no-results" class="no-results" hidden>No findings match these filters. Try a broader search.</div></section>

<section id="usage"><div class="eyebrow">03 / Personalized recommendations</div><h2>What your recorded workflow suggests</h2><p class="section-intro">90,973 retained Atuin records span 5 September 2025 through 26 October 2026. The analysis keeps recognized command names and selected subcommands, with no arguments or raw history in this report. Counts are useful signals, not complete execution telemetry.</p>
<div class="usage-panel"><div class="chart-top"><h3>Leading-command records by workflow</h3><label><span class="visually-hidden">History period</span><select id="period"><option value="all">All retained history</option><option value="30d">Last 30 days</option><option value="7d">Last 7 days</option></select></label></div><div id="usage-chart"></div><p class="small muted">Aliases are grouped where their configuration is known. Bar lengths compare counts within the selected period; there is no implied productivity or error score.</p><noscript><p>All-time records: Git/g 16,371; Neovim commands 10,330; Terraform commands and aliases 4,499; kubectl/k 3,292; rg 3,239; curl 2,216; update 733.</p></noscript></div>
<div class="grid2" style="margin-top:18px"><div class="tile"><h3>Herdr is already the main terminal workflow</h3><div class="num-row"><div><b>{AI['herdr_saved_workspaces']}</b><span>saved workspaces</span></div><div><b>{AI['herdr_saved_tabs']}</b><span>saved tabs</span></div><div><b>{AI['herdr_saved_panes']}</b><span>saved panes</span></div></div><p>Only seven explicit <code>herdr</code> commands appear in retained shell history. That cannot measure keyboard shortcuts, launchers, integrations or long-lived sessions. The saved layout and declarative integration are much more useful evidence here.</p></div><div class="tile"><h3>Separate tool installation from proven adoption</h3><div class="num-row"><div><b>4,825</b><span>retained OpenCode sessions</span></div><div><b>9.33 GiB</b><span>two OpenCode databases</span></div></div><p>These are historical rows, including child sessions, not active concurrent work. OpenRig’s database has zero rigs, nodes and sessions. Paperclip has hourly backups configured and 71 backup files, but no restore was tested.</p></div></div>
<div class="grid2" style="margin-top:18px"><div class="tile"><h3>CLI and editor priorities</h3><ol class="insight-list">{usage_recs}</ol></div><div class="tile"><h3>Herdr and agent-tool priorities</h3><ol class="insight-list">{ai_recs}</ol></div></div>
<details class="panel"><summary>How to interpret the usage data</summary>{paras(D['cli_usage']['methodology'])}<p class="small">Recorded nonzero exits were not treated as failures. Interrupts, search misses and Terraform detailed-exitcode outcomes make that inference unreliable. Missing history is not evidence that a tool should be removed.</p></details></section>

<section id="roadmap"><div class="eyebrow">04 / Suggested order of work</div><h2>A practical sequence</h2><p class="section-intro">Keep each change small enough to attribute its effect. Priorities below preserve independent flakes, passwordless-update convenience where desired, and the existing working desktop.</p>
<div class="roadmap"><div class="step"><h3>Make recovery instructions trustworthy</h3><p>Resolve stable per-host disk identity and repair the installer recipe before it is used. Document backup coverage and one demonstrated restore. Add a tested kernel recovery entry.</p><p><a href="#SYS-01">SYS-01</a> · <a href="#SYS-05">SYS-05</a> · <a href="#SYS-06">SYS-06</a> · <a href="#SYS-09">SYS-09</a></p><p class="acceptance">Done when: a disposable VM rehearsal reaches first boot, the target links and secret paths survive chroot, and a representative file/database restore works. Physical disk identity is verified separately on each laptop.</p></div><div class="step"><h3>Repair bounded integration defects</h3><p>Quote or remove evaluated Slack token serialization, use token-file support for tunnels, fix Pi’s Herdr skill link, and make optional remote access stop retrying when unconfigured.</p><p><a href="#AI-001">AI-001</a> · <a href="#AI-002">AI-002</a> · <a href="#AI-003">AI-003</a> · <a href="#AI-008">AI-008</a></p><p class="acceptance">Done when: synthetic metacharacters stay data, required assets are readable, secrets are absent from argv, and the tunnel is deliberately inactive or stably running.</p></div><div class="step"><h3>Align the editor with daily work</h3><p>Select nixfmt explicitly and repair both formatting-save callbacks. Then evaluate Terraform/YAML language support and document the working distinction between Neovim splits and Herdr panes.</p><p><a href="#ECLI-001">ECLI-001</a> · <a href="#ECLI-002">ECLI-002</a> · <a href="#ECLI-003">ECLI-003</a> · <a href="#ECLI-008">ECLI-008</a></p><p class="acceptance">Done when: a temporary buffer uses the expected formatter, the first toggle disables formatting, project tool versions are intentional, and pane navigation has a documented tested path.</p></div><div class="step"><h3>Choose and document trust policies</h3><p>Decide which networks should reach SSH and which branches may auto-run environment code. Keep or change root-equivalent update convenience explicitly. Review browser/clipboard persistence in the same pass.</p><p><a href="#SYS-02">SYS-02</a> · <a href="#SYS-03">SYS-03</a> · <a href="#ECLI-007">ECLI-007</a> · <a href="#DESK-01">DESK-01</a> · <a href="#DESK-02">DESK-02</a></p><p class="acceptance">Done when: the intended boundaries are written down, a second client confirms the SSH behavior, and synthetic clipboard/profile tests match the chosen retention policy.</p></div><div class="step"><h3>Make upgrades easier to diagnose</h3><p>Prebuild both layers, preserve pins through activation, bring the OpenCode launcher under declarative ownership, repair small CLI helpers, and retire stale schema keys, shortcuts and dependency aliases.</p><p><a href="#ECLI-005">ECLI-005</a> · <a href="#AI-004">AI-004</a> · <a href="#ECLI-010">ECLI-010</a> · <a href="#DESK-06">DESK-06</a> · <a href="#DESK-08">DESK-08</a></p><p class="acceptance">Done when: failure fixtures leave understandable state, effective tools match the selected profile, and focused dry builds produce only known, justified warnings.</p></div><div class="step"><h3>Run controlled hardware experiments</h3><p>Remove the unsupported TLP knobs, measure the active disk policy, and test UCSI/GPU warnings against real peripherals. Compare browser tuning on AC and battery before adopting more flags.</p><p><a href="#SYS-08">SYS-08</a> · <a href="#SYS-10">SYS-10</a> · <a href="#SYS-12">SYS-12</a> · <a href="#DESK-04">DESK-04</a></p><p class="acceptance">Done when: each retained setting has a supported interface, an observed effect, a hardware/kernel scope and a rollback path. A quieter journal alone is not a performance measurement.</p></div></div></section>

<section id="validation"><div class="eyebrow">05 / Verification record</div><h2>What was actually checked</h2><p class="section-intro">Successful evaluations and isolated reproductions support the concrete findings. Hardware changes, real cloud operations and data-restoration exercises remain future validation tasks.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><caption class="visually-hidden">Audit checks and results</caption><thead><tr><th style="width:24%">Check</th><th style="width:18%">Outcome</th><th>Evidence and limits</th></tr></thead><tbody>{check_rows}</tbody></table></div>
<div class="review-summary"><h3>Independent review changed the emphasis</h3><ul><li>The disk hazard is scoped to destructive installation, not ordinary updates.</li><li>Passwordless Nix is an intentional root trust choice; preserving it is a valid option.</li><li>Terraform/YAML support, a two-layer prebuild and an offline Terraform fallback are improvements, not demonstrated failures.</li><li>TPM enrollment details were not read; unsigned boot observations do not prove the current unlock path.</li><li>UCSI and battery observations are presented without claiming untested hardware symptoms.</li></ul></div>
<h3 style="margin-top:28px">Keep these strengths</h3>{strengths}</section>

<section id="inventory"><div class="eyebrow">06 / Scope and version evidence</div><h2>Two flakes, one workstation</h2><div class="architecture"><div class="arch-lane"><strong>nixos/flake.nix</strong><div class="arch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><p>Shared baseline + machine profile</p><p>Kernel · storage · network · power · system services</p><p><b>Two independent host outputs</b></p></div><div class="arch-lane"><strong>home-manager/flake.nix</strong><div class="arch-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div><p>User modules + pinned tooling</p><p>Neovim · CLI · Herdr · AI tools · GNOME · GUI</p><p><b>One user output: nelson</b></p></div></div><p class="small muted">Both root nixpkgs inputs currently resolve to <code>3ec636362e18</code>. Home Manager’s root points to the lock node named <code>nixpkgs_2</code>; an older transitive node named <code>nixpkgs</code> is not the user layer’s root package set. No recommendation merges these flakes.</p>
<div class="grid2"><div class="tile"><h3>Observed current host</h3><p>LG Gram Pro 17 (2025) · kernel {esc(SYS['kernel_running'])} · systemd {esc(SYS['systemd_version'])} · TLP {esc(SYS['tlp_version'])}</p><p>About 30 GiB RAM · 15.4 GiB zram · 52% root usage · 27% of the 2 GiB ESP used at the recorded snapshot.</p><p>17.16 s total boot, including firmware/loader; 5.307 s to graphical.target in userspace. Battery gauge estimate: 76.4% of design; the separate 80% charge cap works.</p></div><div class="tile"><h3>Editor and desktop</h3><p>Neovim {esc(E['neovim_version'])} · Herdr {esc(AI['herdr_installed_version'])} · GNOME 50.4 · Chrome 156.0.8078.47</p><p>76 plugin directories (36 eager, 40 lazy). One isolated headless startup sample was about 129 ms; this is context, not an interactive latency benchmark.</p><p>131 Home Manager package entries and 14 active GNOME extensions. Package entries do not equal transitive closure size.</p></div></div>
<details class="panel"><summary>GNOME extension support metadata · all 14 active</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Extension</th><th>Declared shell versions</th><th>Shell 50 metadata</th><th>Runtime</th></tr></thead><tbody>{extension_rows}</tbody></table></div></details>
<details class="panel"><summary>Direct flake inputs and locked revisions</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Input</th><th>Revision / tarball</th><th>Source modified</th></tr></thead><tbody>{input_rows}</tbody></table></div><p class="small muted">Source dates are metadata, not the date this workstation was updated. The lock files include their integrity hashes; no input was refreshed.</p></details>
<details class="panel"><summary>File inventory and reviewed-snapshot fingerprints · {len(D['inventory'])} entries</summary><p class="small">{D['tracked_files']} tracked files, including {D['nix_files']} Nix files. Inventory below includes configuration, scripts and selected documentation. Dependency lock contents and binary assets were not subjected to a full transitive supply-chain audit.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Review area</th><th>SHA-256 prefix</th></tr></thead><tbody>{inventory_rows}</tbody></table></div></details></section>

<section id="method"><div class="eyebrow">07 / Provenance and limits</div><h2>How to read this review</h2><div class="method-list">{methodology}</div><div class="callout"><b>Existing work was preserved.</b><p>All original tracked-file hashes match the initial review snapshot. The seven pre-existing edited files remain yours. This delivery adds only the report folder.</p></div><details class="panel"><summary>Initial working-tree changes</summary><pre class="small">{esc(D['initial_status'])}</pre></details>{limitations}<p class="small muted">The report is fully local: no analytics, remote fonts, external JavaScript or automatic requests. Primary-source links open only when you follow them. Review notes use local browser storage when available; export your decisions for a portable copy. A printable view expands the full report.</p></section>
<footer class="footer">Nix Lifestyle configuration review · 26 October 2026 · snapshot <code>{esc(D['commit'][:12])}</code> + working edits.<br>Evidence JSON and this HTML are the durable deliverables. Temporary paths in evidence identify audit provenance; their relevant observations are preserved in each finding.<br><a href="report-data.json" download>Download full evidence JSON</a> · <a href="#overview">Return to assessment ↑</a></footer></main>
'''

JS = '''
const AUDIT = __DATA__;
const $ = id => document.getElementById(id);
const cards = [...document.querySelectorAll('.finding')];
const key = 'nix-lifestyle-review-2026-10-26-' + AUDIT.commit.slice(0,12);
let decisions = {};
let storageAvailable = true;
try { const loaded = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || '{}'); if (loaded && typeof loaded === 'object' && !Array.isArray(loaded)) decisions = loaded; } catch { storageAvailable = false; }
const validStates = new Set(['unreviewed','fix','investigate','keep','defer']);
function status(id) { return validStates.has(decisions[id]?.state) ? decisions[id].state : 'unreviewed'; }
function save() {
  try { localStorage.setItem(key,JSON.stringify(decisions)); $('save-status').textContent='Review choices saved in this browser. Export to keep a portable copy.'; }
  catch { storageAvailable=false; $('save-status').textContent='Browser storage is unavailable. Your choices last for this page session; export them before closing.'; }
}
const textIndex = new Map(AUDIT.findings.map(f => [f.id, [f.id,f.title,f.summary,f.impact,f.recommendation,f.validation,f.group,f.category,f.kind,...f.evidence.map(e=>e.file+' '+e.detail)].join(' ').toLowerCase()]));
function applyFilters() {
  const query=$('search').value.trim().toLowerCase().split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean); let count=0;
  for(const c of cards) {
    const visible=query.every(q=>textIndex.get(c.dataset.id).includes(q)) && (!$('priority').value || c.dataset.priority===$('priority').value) && (!$('group').value || c.dataset.group===$('group').value) && (!$('lens').value || c.dataset.lens===$('lens').value) && (!$('review-filter').value || status(c.dataset.id)===$('review-filter').value);
    c.hidden=!visible;if(visible)count++;c.classList.toggle('reviewed',status(c.dataset.id)!=='unreviewed');
  }
  const reviewed=cards.filter(c=>status(c.dataset.id)!=='unreviewed').length;
  $('result-count').textContent=`${count} of ${cards.length} findings · ${reviewed} reviewed`;
  $('no-results').hidden=count!==0;
}
for(const el of document.querySelectorAll('.decision')) {
  const id=el.dataset.for;el.value=status(id);
  el.addEventListener('change',()=>{decisions[id]={...decisions[id],state:el.value};save();applyFilters();});
}
for(const el of document.querySelectorAll('.review-note')) {
  const id=el.dataset.for;el.value=typeof decisions[id]?.note==='string'?decisions[id].note:'';
  el.addEventListener('input',()=>{decisions[id]={...decisions[id],note:el.value};save();});
}
for(const id of ['search','group','priority','lens','review-filter']) $(id).addEventListener(id==='search'?'input':'change',applyFilters);
function resetFilters(){for(const id of ['search','group','priority','lens','review-filter'])$(id).value='';applyFilters();}
$('reset').addEventListener('click',resetFilters);
$('expand').addEventListener('click',()=>cards.filter(c=>!c.hidden).forEach(c=>c.querySelector('.finding-detail').open=true));
$('collapse').addEventListener('click',()=>cards.filter(c=>!c.hidden).forEach(c=>c.querySelector('.finding-detail').open=false));
$('export').addEventListener('click',()=>{
  const items=AUDIT.findings.filter(f=>status(f.id)!=='unreviewed'||decisions[f.id]?.note).map(f=>({id:f.id,title:f.title,priority:f.severity,decision:status(f.id),note:decisions[f.id]?.note||''}));
  const blob=new Blob([JSON.stringify({report:AUDIT.title,snapshot:AUDIT.commit,exportedAt:new Date().toISOString(),decisions:items},null,2)],{type:'application/json'});
  const url=URL.createObjectURL(blob);const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='nix-lifestyle-review-decisions.json';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000);
});
function revealHash(){const id=decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1));const c=cards.find(c=>c.id===id);if(!c)return;resetFilters();c.querySelector('.finding-detail').open=true;requestAnimationFrame(()=>c.scrollIntoView({block:'start'}));}
window.addEventListener('hashchange',revealHash);
document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.key==='/'&&!['INPUT','TEXTAREA','SELECT'].includes(document.activeElement.tagName)){e.preventDefault();$('search').focus();$('search').scrollIntoView({block:'center'});}});
const workflowGroups=[['Git / g',['git','g']],['Neovim',['vim','nvim','vi']],['Terraform',['terraform','t','ta','ti','tp','tpwb','tss']],['Kubernetes',['kubectl','k']],['Ripgrep',['rg']],['curl',['curl']],['update',['update']]];
function drawChart(){const period=$('period').value;const rows=period==='all'?AUDIT.usage.commands:AUDIT.usage.recent_command_counts[period];const vals=workflowGroups.map(([name,keys])=>({name,value:keys.reduce((s,k)=>s+(rows[k]||0),0)}));const max=Math.max(...vals.map(v=>v.value),1);$('usage-chart').replaceChildren();for(const v of vals){const row=document.createElement('div');row.className='bar-row';const label=document.createElement('span');label.textContent=v.name;const track=document.createElement('div');track.className='bar-track';track.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true');const fill=document.createElement('div');fill.className='bar-fill';fill.style.width=(v.value/max*100)+'%';track.append(fill);const number=document.createElement('span');number.className='bar-value';number.textContent=v.value.toLocaleString();row.append(label,track,number);$('usage-chart').append(row);}}
$('period').addEventListener('change',drawChart);drawChart();
let printState=null;
window.addEventListener('beforeprint',()=>{printState={details:[...document.querySelectorAll('details')].map(e=>[e,e.open]),hidden:cards.map(e=>[e,e.hidden])};document.querySelectorAll('details').forEach(e=>e.open=true);cards.forEach(e=>e.hidden=false);});
window.addEventListener('afterprint',()=>{if(!printState)return;printState.details.forEach(([e,o])=>e.open=o);printState.hidden.forEach(([e,h])=>e.hidden=h);printState=null;});
for(const id of ['print-main','print-side'])$(id).addEventListener('click',()=>window.print());
if(!storageAvailable)$('save-status').textContent='Browser storage is unavailable. Export review choices before closing this page.';
applyFilters();revealHash();
window.auditUI={applyFilters,resetFilters,drawChart,getDecisions:()=>decisions};
'''.replace('__DATA__', json.dumps(dict(title=D['title'],commit=D['commit'],findings=[{k:v for k,v in f.items() if k not in ['sources']} for f in F],usage=D['cli_usage']), ensure_ascii=True).replace('</','<\\/'))

OUTPUT='<!doctype html>\n<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><meta name="description" content="Local evidence-based NixOS, Home Manager, Neovim, Herdr and CLI configuration review."><title>Nix Lifestyle — Configuration Review</title><style>'+CSS+'</style></head><body>'+BODY+'<script>'+JS+'</script></body></html>\n'
(HERE/'index.html').write_text(OUTPUT)
print(f'Rendered {len(F)} findings, {len(CHECKS)} checks, {len(OUTPUT):,} characters')
